{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implemented and pushed for review: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1505\n\n## Every removal was proved against the resolver, not assumed\n\n| removal | evidence |\n|---|---|\n| `inspect-ai>=0.3.221` + the whole `[eval]` extra | zero `import inspect_ai` in `src/`; the one hit was the `_optional.EXTRAS` name string |\n| both `[tool.uv] conflicts` entries | `uv lock` regenerates clean; `uv sync --locked --extra dev --extra bedrock` **installs** — the pair the fork previously forbade. `--extra agents` and `--extra dev --extra agents` also install |\n| `override-dependencies = [\"click>=8.3.3\"]` | regenerated lock resolves **click 8.4.2** unaided; `pip-audit` over the locked `dev` env: `No known vulnerabilities found` |\n| the now-empty `[tool.uv]` table | nothing else used it |\n\nNothing turned out to be load-bearing for a non-inspect-ai reason, so no piece was\nkept back.\n\n## The `[eval]` extra: removed, not emptied and not aliased\n\ninspect-ai was its only member. The offline prompt-eval surface (`rebar prompt eval`,\nspec validation, grader discipline, coverage, JUnit) is stdlib-only and needs no\nextra; the live run goes through rebar's own solver on the pydantic-ai runtime — the\n`[agents]` extra, which `_live_solver` already documented as its real requirement.\nRedefining `[eval]` as an alias for `[agents]` was rejected: it would make\n`extra_installed(\"eval\")` a synonym for a capability that already has a name, which is\nthe machinery this change deletes.\n\nEvery place that told a reader the live run needs `[eval]` now names `agents`: the two\nCLI hints, seven eval-spec headers, three test docstrings, and `prompt-eval.yml`\n(header comment, job name, step name, and the `uv sync` itself, now `--extra agents`).\n\n## Also fixed\n\n`src/rebar/llm/evals/eval.py`'s module docstring made the Inspect AI claim **twice**\n(lines 6 and 21), both contradicted by the implementation comment above the live-run\nsection in the same file. Rewritten to describe the native solver loop that actually\nruns. Dead `INSPECT_MIN_VERSION` deleted.\n\n## Gate\n\n`make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the full suite (11148 passed, 49 skipped) are green,\nplus the new `tests/unit/test_packaging_dependencies.py` — which pins the four removals\nand adds the inverse guard that every `_optional.EXTRAS` name resolves to a real\ndeclared extra, so the registry can never again advertise an install that does nothing.\n\nBreaking change documented in `CHANGELOG.md` (Unreleased) and `docs/release-notes.md`."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786117849741172001,"uuid":"b4cd577a-8124-4863-b2b3-d1525950976a"}